        "date": "2026-10-21T18:41:02Z"
      },
      "message": "Place batch 204: six unique 215-state alternatives, retire 9 archives\n\nDiscard essential duplicates, preserve unique alternatives (direction for\nthese batches). All 578 incoming .tm tables were put in rooted breadth-first\ncanonical form and compared with every repository table and with each other.\n\nPlaced as delivered (byte-identical, nothing rerun) under\ncandidate-k215/alternatives/, each with an INTAKE.md:\n- dr215 (DR215_research, 2a11b6d29f): direct transfer + rho6 permutation,\n  repaired strong selector. late_comparison/ (ZC215 copies) omitted.\n- forced-transfer (FT215_Forced_Transfer, 6101f25c72): S;W(0);S;W(1);...\n  scheduler, conservative debt seven. cache216/, composite216/ omitted.\n- zero-credit (ZC215_Research, a10b2c302c): DROP 0 / NIP 1 tags and\n  exhaustive enumeration; NIP->DROP lowering injects pops into earlier pushes,\n  so no AX stack credit is needed. reference/ (parent copies) omitted.\n- gc215 (ZFC_GC215, dfe1f22bdf): the AX tag as generalization binder, paid\n  for by a conditional decoder merge. reference/ (corpus, gc216) omitted.\n- context-returns (ZFC_K215_Context_Transfers, b6fb232916): history-dependent\n  decoder returns; k215-context and the principal k215-shallow (depth 46).\n  upstream/ (K215 copies) omitted.\n- gc-zc215 (Proof_Simplification_and_GC-ZC215, 05d063acef): gc215 combined\n  with zero-credit enumeration; zc215 copies and the inert 216 allocation\n  omitted. Its proof_refactor/ goes to k225-formal/verification/k215/\n  simplification/proposal-2026-10-21/ with an INTAKE.md recording which\n  proposals main already realizes (Lean OBisim.symm) and which are open\n  (Rocq mirror check, compact Rocq certificate).\n\nRetired without placement:\n- ZFC_ST215_Rho6_and_New_Routes (b872b34ff4): the same table as dr215.\n- NW215_counter_stack (dfe1f22bdf): K215's source conjugated by the register\n  permutation 0 <-> 2, a renaming of registers.\n- SB215_ZFC (2a11b6d29f): refuted. The correction review shipped in\n  gc-zc215/correction/ shows that in SB215 and SB215-AB the return after AX\n  reaches selector ordinal 23, not the scheduler, so the NIP test halts on\n  cache 1 from the blank tape.\n\nAdds six index rows and the batch-204 queue entry. No numbered Sources, no\nwrite report; the queue is clear.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
